  "T1_page_vs_line": "HOLDS: mode follows section and page (section 12% vs null 1%, page-within-section 13% vs 4%, both transcriptions); Bio/quire M is q-heavy; effect sits in Currier B (illus eta2 0.15) not A (0.03); hand adds little within language. Italian pseudo-pages: 2% / 7% vs 4.6%.",
  "line_level_mode": "WEAK: after removing the page mean, first and second halves of a line correlate only r=0.06-0.07 (Italian 0.08, Latin 0.01). Most of the mode signal is page-level, not a per-line switch.",
  "T2_positions": "HOLDS (small): in mixed lines q-words sit earlier and a-words later (mean position gap -0.045, z -7, both transcriptions, also interior-only, stronger in A); prose controls 0 to +0.016; self-citation null. Not a two-column table: gap is 5% of the line.",
  "T3_templates": "FAILS: class templates are no more concentrated than an interior shuffle (deficit 0.02-0.03 bits with 3 classes, 0.00 with 5 classes); Dante verse gives 0.075 bits (z 7). Markov-3 deficit is only the line-mode clumping.",
  "T4_edges": "HOLDS: first and last words are special vocabularies beyond their edge glyph (z ~30, excess MI 0.057-0.067 bits vs Italian 0.014-0.030, Latin 0.009-0.024; Dante last-word 0.21 from rhyme). Line-final q-words are rare (8.6% vs 16%). The word before a final -m word is a-class 33-35% vs 24% shuffled (z 6-7).",
  "T5_controls": "self_citation reproduces none of T1 section effect, T2, T4; it over-produces page drift."
 }
